=== PORTABILITY PROOF ===
The committed kernels/generated/*.cu (emitted by --lower-to-cuda, T8/T14) are
compiled UNCHANGED by hipcc with -DPOLYKERNEL_HIP --offload-arch=gfx1101. The
SAME .cu that nvcc builds with -DPOLYKERNEL_CUDA compiles under hipcc, because
every kernel targets kernels/template/kernel_common.h and uses only the portable
pk_* / PK_* names (the backend is selected by the -D define, never by a source edit).

=== ONE GENUINE PORTABILITY GUARD ADDED (documented, no numerics change) ===
kernel_common.h defined PK_FULL_MASK as 0xffffffffu (32-bit). CUDA __shfl_*_sync
take a 32-bit mask, but HIP __shfl_*_sync are templates that static_assert
sizeof(mask)==8 (HIP supports wave32 AND wave64 -> 64-bit mask). Without a guard,
hipcc errors: "The mask must be a 64-bit integer" (reproduced in scratch in
reports/w4_hipcc_portability_neg.log). Fix: PK_FULL_MASK is now backend-guarded —
0xffffffffu on CUDA (UNCHANGED), 0xffffffffffffffffull on HIP. This is a
lane-participation mask only (all lanes enabled either way); reduction numerics
are identical. After this one guard, ALL 7 kernels compile clean.

